  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Drought Mitigation in Kiribati</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to address severe drought conditions in Kiribati through interventions focused on enhancing water security, ensuring equitable access to clean water, and fostering social and behaviour changes for safe hygiene practices. &#x202f;Leveraging the International Organization for Migration&apos;s (IOM) expertise and operational capacities in the Pacific region, the intervention pivots towards prioritizing resilience-building measures, early recovery, and disaster risk reduction strategies, aligned with the Early Recovery, Risk Reduction, and Resilience (ER4) framework. IOM presence in the region enables a strategic entry into Kiribati to address the worsening drought situation with initial emphasis on water security, especially safe water storage, treatment, and driving social and behaviour change. IOM&apos;s interventions aim to bolster community self-reliance, preparing them to mitigate and respond to hazards &amp; disaster events through capacity-building and resilience-building measures. &#x202f;IOM&apos;s evidence-based, risk-informed approach focuses on fortifying early warning systems, improving disaster preparedness, and strengthening first-responder capabilities. These efforts are vital in reinforcing national disaster risk management capacities and fostering resilience within at-risk communities to promote self-reliance.</narrative>
  </description>
